==Welsh==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|cy|wlm|porffor}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-bry-pro|*porfor}}, from {{der|cy|la|purpura||purple}} (compare {{cog|sga|corcur}}, modern {{cog|ga|corcra}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|cy|/ˈpɔrfɔr/}}
* {{rhymes|cy|ɔrfɔr|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{cy-adj|mwy}}

# [[purple]]
#* 1918''', {{w|Hedd Wyn}}, "Atgo":
#*: Dim ond lleuad '''borffor''' / Ar fin y mynydd llwm; / A sŵn hen afon Prysor / Yn canu yn y Cwm.
#*:: Only a '''purple''' moon / On the edge of the bare mountain; / And the sound of the old river Prysor / Singing in the Valley.
